Incident Overview:
The primary server(server-1) experienced a total
network isolation due to misconfigured static IP.
This blockage prevented the installation of the (cockpit-pcp) metrics packag and halted all system repository updates.

2.Diagnostic Findings
Routing issue: The server lacked a vaild route to the external gateaway.
DNS conflict: System-resolved conflicts prevented consistent name resolution,resulting in
"Could not resolve" errors during upate attempts.

3.Remediation Strategy
Dynamic Addressing: Reconfigured the Netplan YAML to (dhcp4: true) for the (enp1s0) interface.
Force Lease renewal: Executed (sudo dhclinet -v enp1s0) to obtain a vaild IP within the host's
subnet (172.20.10.5).
DNS Hardening: injected 8.8.8.8 as the primary nameserver to bypass local resolution faliures.

4.Conclusion
The server successfully established an external uplink.All system package were upgraded,
and the Cockpit web interface
is now fully operational with active performance metrics.
